From 5036b7e8a61c4cf1e18abad8746208d03d268ea5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:07:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(launch): expose explicitly assigned virtual null devices

Use the existing device registry for an immutable virtual /dev view,
with bounded null-device descriptors and controlled metadata copies.
Resolve image aliases through the same namespace as storage so hidden
image devices never become a native fallback.

Keep descriptor ownership distinct, preserve empty-path memory/native
metadata, and cover access modes, flags, isolation and exhaustion.

Signed-off-by: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
